<title>FINLAND: NOKIA FALLS SHARPLY AS DOLLAR WEAKENS.</title>
<headline>NOKIA FALLS SHARPLY AS DOLLAR WEAKENS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish telecommunications group Nokia fell sharply on Fridday, hit by dollar weakness and weak Treasuries, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1630/1330 GMT, Nokia traded at 471.00 markka, down 21.00 markka or over four percent. Volume in the stock was just under half the bourse total of around 730 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been such a sharp rise, investors take profits as soon as they get a reason to,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 248</p>
</text>
